\f1\b\fs56 \cf0 Executive Summary\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Your profile suggests a leader who may be:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Moderately confident without being strongly self-focused (Narcissism 46).\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Relatively strategic, political, and outcomes-oriented (Machiavellianism 64).\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Comfortable making difficult decisions, tolerating conflict, and maintaining emotional distance when necessary (Psychopathy 68).\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Not especially motivated by causing discomfort to others (Sadism 43).\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Capable of understanding and considering others' perspectives (Empathy 61).\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Strongly inclined toward modesty, learning, and not needing to be the focal point (Humility 75).\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Generally guided by ethical considerations in leadership (Ethical Leadership 68).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The most interesting feature is the combination of:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Higher humility and empathy\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Moderately high ethical leadership\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Alongside relatively elevated strategic pragmatism and emotional toughness\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 In practice, this can produce a leader who is able to make difficult decisions and remain composed under pressure, while still caring about fairness and team outcomes. The developmental challenge is ensuring that decisiveness does not drift into excessive detachment, and that strategic thinking does not unintentionally reduce transparency or trust.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
